# NOTICE — Third-Party Derivative Sources

This file records third-party sources from which OnePage firmware code is derived, copied, or adapted, to satisfy
upstream open-source license obligations. It complements the project `LICENSE` (MIT, which preserves the original
CrossPoint Reader copyright).

## Upstream project

- **CrossPoint Reader** — https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader — MIT License.
  OnePage firmware is a port of CrossPoint Reader for the OnePage ESP32-C61 board. Copyright is retained in `LICENSE`.

## CrossMux (planned derivative source)

- **CrossMux** — https://github.com/0x1abin/crossmux — MIT License. A community fork of CrossPoint Reader.
  OnePage has repositioned its apps/tools platform to align with CrossMux; selected CrossMux features will be brought in
  via **feature-by-feature vendor-and-port** (see `docs/crossmux-port-analysis.md`).

### Current status

- The **online dictionary downloader** has been vendored and ported from CrossMux (see the register below). Each ported
  file keeps the `Ported from CrossMux … modified by OnePage.` header line.
- Everything else that merely looks CrossMux-flavoured is still OnePage-authored code *modeled on* CrossMux's design
  language (the `Tools`/`ToolApp`/`ToolsUi` code and comments referencing "crossmux-style"). That is original work and
  needs no per-file upstream copyright.
- A compiled CrossMux firmware binary is used only as a web download artifact
  (`web/public/firmware/crossmux-onepage.bin`), not source.

### Attribution policy for future ports (Phase 2+)

When a file is copied or adapted from CrossMux, before it is merged:

1. Keep CrossMux's original copyright notice and MIT permission text at the top of the copied/adapted file. If the file
   has substantial OnePage modifications, add a `Ported from CrossMux (https://github.com/0x1abin/crossmux), MIT License;
   modified by OnePage.` line under the retained notice.
2. Append a one-line entry to the register below (component, source path, commit/date).
3. If the port constitutes a large body of incorporated source, a corresponding
   `Copyright (c) <year> CrossMux contributors` line may be added to `LICENSE` alongside the existing copyright holders.

MIT requires the copyright notice and permission notice be included in all copies or substantial portions of the software.

